message.content:
This is a traffic signal system, a functional unit under Note 4 to Section XVI. Traffic signals for pedestrian control fall under heading 8530, "Electrical signaling, safety or traffic control equipment for railways, tramways, roads, inland waterways, parking facilities, port installations or airfields (other than those of heading 8608)." Subheading 8530.80 covers "Other equipment," and its statistical suffix is 8530.80.0000. 8530.10 is for railways or tramways and 8530.80 is for other equipment, so 8530.80.00 applies. Its 10-digit form is 8530.80.0000.

CBP rulings on LED pedestrian signal modules have gone both ways: some classify them under 8531.20 (indicator panels with LEDs), while others classify them under 8530.80. Because this system controls traffic, 8530.80 is the better fit.

{"hts_code": "8530.80.0000", "reason": "The pedestrian signal system (display, control and interface units) is a functional unit under Section XVI Note 4 and constitutes electrical traffic control equipment for roads of heading 8530, falling under the 'other' subheading 8530.80."}
